# UI spacing & chrome

Dark + mint product UI. Prefer theme tokens (`bg-background`, `bg-primary`, etc.) over hardcoded hex.

## App shell
- Content: `max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4`
- Main vertical rhythm: `pt-4 space-y-4`
- Centered load/error states: `p-4 text-center space-y-3`
- Search → list: same `space-y-4`; no `border-b` / `shadow` divider under the search bar
- Sticky search (tracks only) may keep `bg-background/95 backdrop-blur-md`, but no extra `py-3` chrome that changes the gap vs requests

## Lists
- Gap between rows: `space-y-2.5` (or `pb-2.5` inside collapse clips)
- Cards: `rounded-xl … px-4 py-3 … gap-3`
- Title → artist: `mt-1`
- Empty states: `my-2 space-y-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/80 bg-card/50 p-8 text-center`

## Modals (`ModalShell`)
- Header: `px-5 py-4` — icon tile + title; always include corner `X` close
- Body: `p-5` (confirm copy lives here, not only in the header)
- Footer: `p-4` — primary then cancel
- Playlist filter toolbar/list: also `p-5`

## Controls
- Modal primary / destructive confirm: `px-5 py-2.5 rounded-xl`
- Modal cancel / secondary: `px-4 py-2 rounded-xl`
- Filter chips & compact clears: `px-3 py-1.5 rounded-xl`
- Text inputs / selects: `px-3.5 py-2.5 rounded-xl`

## Do not
- Mix `space-y-2` list gaps with `pb-2.5` list gaps in the same product surface
- Use `px-4 py-2` for primary actions (that padding is for cancel/secondary)
- Put confirm body text only in the modal header
